---
title: Sequence Diagram - low risk fund transfer (FR-07)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant UI as React front end
    participant SEC as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant TC as TransactionController
    participant TS as TransactionService
    participant FR as FraudRiskService
    participant AR as AccountRepository
    participant NS as NotificationService
    participant AS as AuditService
    participant DB as Database

    C->>UI: Fill transfer form, press Review
    UI->>C: Show confirmation panel
    C->>UI: Press Confirm and transfer
    UI->>SEC: POST /api/transactions/transfer + Bearer token
    SEC->>SEC: Verify signature and expiry
    SEC->>TC: Authenticated request (role CUSTOMER)
    TC->>TC: Bean Validation on the request body
    TC->>TS: transfer(request)

    TS->>DB: Find source account owned by this customer
    DB-->>TS: Account
    TS->>TS: Check account ACTIVE, not a self-transfer
    TS->>DB: Sum amount reserved by pending transfers
    DB-->>TS: Reserved amount
    TS->>TS: available = balance minus reserved, check it is sufficient
    TS->>DB: Look for an identical transfer in the last 60 seconds
    DB-->>TS: None found

    Note over TS,FR: Risk is assessed BEFORE the row is stored, so the<br/>transfer is not counted against itself by the velocity rule
    TS->>FR: evaluate(account, beneficiary, amount, now)
    FR->>DB: Count recent transfers and failed verifications
    DB-->>FR: Counts
    FR-->>TS: score 0, level LOW, no factors fired

    TS->>DB: Save transaction (status PENDING, risk LOW)
    TS->>AS: TRANSFER_INITIATED, RISK_EVALUATED
    AS->>DB: Insert audit rows (own transaction)

    rect rgb(230, 244, 236)
        Note over TS,DB: One database transaction: both balances<br/>and the status change commit together (NFR-02)
        TS->>AR: Debit source account
        TS->>AR: Credit destination account if it is internal
        TS->>TS: status = APPROVED, completedAt = now
        AR->>DB: Persist
    end

    TS->>AS: TRANSACTION_APPROVED
    AS->>DB: Insert audit row
    TS->>NS: notify(customer, "Transfer completed")
    NS->>DB: Insert notification
    TS-->>TC: TransactionResponse (APPROVED, LOW, score 0)
    TC-->>UI: 201 Created
    UI->>C: Transaction detail page with the green Approved badge
